# In-Memory Computing for Artificial Intelligence

This case study explains In-Memory Computing (IMC), a computing technology that performs computations directly within memory to reduce data movement between the processor and memory.

It covers the architecture of in-memory computing, different memory technologies, the comparison between conventional computing and in-memory computing, and its execution model.

The case study also discusses AI applications such as deep neural networks, transformers, edge AI, and neuromorphic computing, along with the advantages, limitations, and future potential of this technology.

